{:id :i3-display-scaling-external
 :date "2026-10-26"
 :row :I3
 :claim "Display scaling and external displays: the scale steps run and the text/controls change with them, and a second display is attached and shows the guest's own content."
 :host {:model "MacBookPro18,4", :cpu "Apple M1 Max", :os "Darwin 25.4.0 arm64"}
 :commit "5e8ec9c2bad2f5f8df7decc37e241b6969d06866"
 :verdicts {"scale-steps-executed" {:green? true, :reason :marker, :marker "AIUEOS_GUEST_BROWSER_SCALE_GO events=16 ... AIUEOS_GUEST_BROWSER_SCALE_OK events=16 (scale-steps.txt) - the harness answered every SCALE_GO with its 16-key sequence and the guest consumed all 16 events"}
            "scale-moves-text-and-controls" {:green? true, :reason :evidence, :evidence "scale-steps.txt: pct runs 100 (n=1..3) -> 125 (n=4,5) -> 150 (n=6..9) -> 125 (n=10,11) -> 100 (n=12..16). Each step changes what the desktop draws: vw/vh 1280x800 -> 1024x640 -> 853x533 -> 1024x640 -> 1280x800, text-px 582 -> 1536 -> 1828 -> 1536 -> 582, and the frame-model hash per step 25c93f77 -> 48a15000 -> 67c770b1 -> 48a15000 -> 25c93f77 (matching the gate's model expectations, identical values across repeated identical steps)"}
            "scale-gate-green" {:green? true, :reason :marker, :marker "AIUEOS_COMPOSITOR_GUEST_BROWSER_UI_SCALE_OK - the browser-desktop-ui-scale gate's own verdict, printed after the run it measured (log line of run kbb --backend sci scripts/run-task.cljk browser-desktop-ui-scale with AIUEOS_LOOP_EXIT_OK=1)"}
            "second-display-bound" {:green? true, :reason :marker, :marker "AIUEOS_GUEST_SCANOUT_TWO_OK scanouts=2 resource-0=1 resource-1=2 kotoba-n=2 and AIUEOS_GUEST_GPU_TWO_OK resources=2 flush=2 kotoba-n=2 (scanout-two-run-serial.log) - the guest bound two scanouts, the second one to its own second 2D resource"}
            "second-display-image" {:green? true, :reason :evidence, :evidence "screen-head1.ppm - QMP screendump of head 1: P6 32x32, all 1024 pixels 0x22aa55, the exact fill the kernel writes into its second resource (pixels2[i] = 0xff22aa55U). The host is not reporting an enabled-but-empty output; the image is the guest's own content"}
            "both-heads-host-readback" {:green? true, :reason :evidence, :evidence "screen-head0.ppm (P6 1280x800, top colour f1f1f2 = the desktop background) and external-display-readback.md: the host's DBus names both heads of the same device - aiueosvga.0 Head 0 1280x800 and aiueosvga.1 Head 1 32x32, both pci/0000/06.0"}
            "no-failure-path-hit" {:green? true, :reason :marker, :marker "both serials together contain zero AIUEOS_EVIDENCE_STOP and zero AIUEOS_VIRTIO_GPU_FAIL (scale-run-serial.log stop=0 gpu_fail=0; scanout-two-run-serial.log stop=0 gpu_fail=0)"}}
 :run
 {:mechanism "Two runs of the same worktree, both after commit 5e8ec9c fixed the one thing that had been breaking the stage chain (the C9 status bar covered the pointer's corner test point, so the cursor stage failed one frame and the connected chain never reached SCALE). The scale half is the gate run: kbb --backend sci scripts/run-task.cljk browser-desktop-ui-scale with AIUEOS_LOOP_EXIT_OK=1, because the ui-scale profile leaves that flag unset and the smoke would otherwise hold QEMU for its 6000s wall clock instead of ending at the desktop loop. The external-display half is the scanout-two run: AIUEOS_GUEST_SCANOUT_TWO=1 AIUEOS_GUEST_BROWSER=1 AIUEOS_SMOKE_FINAL_PROBE=0 ./os/aiueos/scripts/smoke-qemu-uefi.sh with AIUEOS_QEMU_TIMEOUT=540, after giving the graphics device an id (-device virtio-vga,id=aiueosvga,disable-legacy=on,max_outputs=2) so QMP screendump could name a head"
  :procedure "scale: build, boot, wait for SCALE_GO, watch the 16 keyed steps land as AIUEOS_GUEST_BROWSER_SCALE n=.. pct=.. lines, then the gate's own verdict line. external display: boot with scanout-two enabled, wait for AIUEOS_GUEST_SCANOUT_TWO_OK, stop the harness injector so this run could hold QMP itself, screendump head 0 and head 1 by device id, read both heads back from the host's DBus"
  :geometry "the physical frame stays the GOP surface 1280x800; the scale changes the LOGICAL viewport inside it (vw/vh 1280x800 at 100% down to 853x533 at 150%), which is why the row's note 'the desktop is fixed at 1280 x 800' still holds for the surface"}
 :caveats
 ["the second display shows the guest's SECOND 32x32 2D resource (ADR-0095), not an extended desktop: nothing is rendered onto that head beyond the resource itself. 'the second display works' is therefore satisfied as 'content the guest chose appears on head 1, verified by image readback', not as a second desktop panel - owner may reject on that reading"
  "the two halves were measured in two separate runs of the same worktree rather than one run: the scale gate and the scanout-two run both boot their own QEMU on the same build directory, so they cannot overlap"
  "the scanout-two run predates the pointer/status-bar fix (5e8ec9c); that fix changes only the order in which the status bar and the pointer are painted, not scanout binding or the second resource, and the scanout-two run had zero failure markers of its own"
  "the external display is a second QEMU virtio-vga head on the reference VM. There is no physical second monitor here; required-level :device evidence for this row is still open"]
 :green? true}
